# The state lines of the format that read what a script reads of a monster and its fight: the npc
# line's mp option and the mp step and check; the want step (an attack desire on a creature,
# holding its ground or walking to it), which the desires check lists in full or short; a hit by a
# member of the party; a servitor of the character as a creature; the reach check of its top
# desire target, and the shows check of an appearance (LV3Orc, 27294, spawns with its weapon glowing at
# +10). The monster is WarriorRunAwayPhysicalSpecial (21508), a fixture of 1000 MP, 60 from the
# character.
character Hunter 20
script script.ai.individual.DefaultNpc
script script.ai.individual.Monster.MonsterAI
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.WarriorBase
script script.ai.individual.Monster.LV3Monster.LV3Monster
script script.ai.individual.Monster.LV3Monster.LV3Orc
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.Warrior
script script.ai.individual.Monster.WarriorBase.Warrior.WarriorRunAwayPhysicalSpecial.WarriorRunAwayPhysicalSpecial
npc wolf 21508 Monster 60 0 0 walks mp 250
npc post 21508 Monster 0 300 0
npc orc 27294 Monster 0 -200 0
member Pal 20
summon pet 14001 servitor 20
roll wolf 0
roll post 0
roll orc 0

advance 1s
  mp wolf 250
  shows wolf rhand=0 lhand=0 glow=0
  shows orc glow=10
mp wolf 40
  mp wolf 40
want wolf player 100 hold
  desires wolf attack(player,hold)=100
  desires wolf attack(player)=100
want wolf pet 70
  desires wolf attack(player,hold)=100 attack(pet)=70
hit wolf 10 by Pal
  hate wolf 125 Pal
hit wolf 10 by pet
  hate wolf 195 pet
top wolf player
  reach wolf yes
top post player
  reach post no
swing wolf
